     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p27-teaching",
     "replacement": "There is no reverse product rule or reverse quotient rule for integration (in the Advanced course).\n\nTo integrate a product such as $x(x+1)$, expand it into separate terms first.\n\nTo integrate a fraction whose denominator is a single term, such as $\\dfrac{3x^4-2x^2}{x^2}$, split it into separate terms first.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p27-teaching",
     "targetFingerprint": "a12c55d3565d30228aa04c6de3cb26ca6c64c9e40f999650548087ae6900e09f",
