     "replacement": "This negative result cannot be correct because the function is always positive. The function is not defined at $x=0$, which lies inside the interval, so the endpoint calculation is invalid.\n\nBefore evaluating, check whether the interval contains a value where you would **divide by zero** or **take an even root of a negative number**. The function is not defined there over the real numbers.",
